{"data": [{"author_id": "702235316812275712", "created_at": "2026-11-03T20:48:36.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2117720623363579961"], "entities": {"mentions": [{"end": 73, "id": "118783936", "start": 58, "username": "keds_economist"}], "urls": [{"description": "Starting Nov 6 at 12:00 PM EST", "display_url": "open.substack.com/live-stream/42…", "end": 169, "expanded_url": "https://open.substack.com/live-stream/428299", "images": [{"height": 480, "url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/news_img/2116905393322651648/NVOb4EG_?format=jpg&name=orig", "width": 920}, {"height": 150, "url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/news_img/2116905393322651648/NVOb4EG_?format=jpg&name=150x150", "width": 150}], "start": 146, "status": 200, "title": "LIVE SOON: Jobs Day with Guy and Keds", "unwound_url": "https://open.substack.com/live-stream/428299", "url": "https://t.co/6F5QbNHiRe"}]}, "id": "2117720623363579961", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 419, "like_count": 2, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "The October jobs report comes out this week, so my friend @keds_economist and I will be in labor market Nerdvana on Friday at 9 AM PT!  Join us:\n\nhttps://t.co/6F5QbNHiRe", "url": "https://x.com/EconBerger/status/2117720623363579961"}, {"author_id": "702235316812275712", "created_at": "2026-11-03T20:24:41.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2117714604273111147"], "entities": {"urls": [{"description": "A Good Month for Workers", "display_url": "macromostly.substack.com/p/jolts-recap-…", "end": 133, "expanded_url": "https://macromostly.substack.com/p/jolts-recap-september-3f0", "images": [{"height": 800, "url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/news_img/2117714606240243712/v4cvHLJi?format=jpg&name=orig", "width": 1600}, {"height": 150, "url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/news_img/2117714606240243712/v4cvHLJi?format=jpg&name=150x150", "width": 150}], "start": 110, "status": 200, "title": "JOLTS Recap (September)", "unwound_url": "https://macromostly.substack.com/p/jolts-recap-september-3f0", "url": "https://t.co/jVlqva69Kr"}, {"display_url": "pic.x.com/cjLMSkR71j", "end": 157, "expanded_url": "https://x.com/EconBerger/status/2117714604273111147/photo/1", "media_key": "3_2117714419669143552", "start": 134, "url": "https://t.co/cjLMSkR71j"}]}, "id": "2117714604273111147", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 2, "impression_count": 897, "like_count": 9, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 2}, "text": "My take on today's JOLTS report - good news that exaggerates the small but genuine recovery in hiring.\n\nLink: https://t.co/jVlqva69Kr https://t.co/cjLMSkR71j", "url": "https://x.com/EconBerger/status/2117714604273111147"}, {"author_id": "3039504459", "created_at": "2026-11-03T20:12:36.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2117711564681695677"], "entities": {"urls": [{"description": "A new formalism yields the quantities that characterize a conventional superconductor without adjustable parameters.", "display_url": "go.aps.org/3Usr4gJ", "end": 274, "expanded_url": "https://go.aps.org/3Usr4gJ", "images": [{"height": 200, "url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/news_img/2117711566757888000/VMZu66sc?format=png&name=orig", "width": 200}, {"height": 150, "url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/news_img/2117711566757888000/VMZu66sc?format=png&name=150x150", "width": 150}], "start": 251, "status": 200, "title": "First-Principles Calculation of Coherence Length and Penetration Depth Based on Density Functional Theory for Superconductors", "unwound_url": "https://journals.aps.org/prl/abstract/10.1103/lrhl-j9bt", "url": "https://t.co/ywwQGeRmB1"}, {"display_url": "pic.x.com/W6vGwWp7rW", "end": 298, "expanded_url": "https://x.com/PhysRevLett/status/2117711564681695677/photo/1", "media_key": "3_2117711561892519936", "start": 275, "url": "https://t.co/W6vGwWp7rW"}]}, "id": "2117711564681695677", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 3, "impression_count": 433, "like_count": 5, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 1, "retweet_count": 1}, "text": "Researchers developed a framework to calculate superconducting coherence lengths and penetration depths without phenomenological parameters, potentially informing the predictive design of new superconductors under extreme conditions.\n\nRead the paper: https://t.co/ywwQGeRmB1 https://t.co/W6vGwWp7rW", "url": "https://x.com/PhysRevLett/status/2117711564681695677"}, {"author_id": "961132338", "created_at": "2026-11-03T20:06:43.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2117710081190203612"], "entities": {"mentions": [{"end": 28, "id": "632091340", "start": 14, "username": "JohnHCochrane"}], "urls": [{"description": "This intriguing substack by André Lara Resende is causing an uproar in Brazil.", "display_url": "grumpy-economist.com/p/fisher-and-r…", "end": 188, "expanded_url": "https://www.grumpy-economist.com/p/fisher-and-resende-in-brazil", "images": [{"height": 800, "url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/news_img/2117690191783796736/yF0xcG2t?format=jpg&name=orig", "width": 1600}, {"height": 150, "url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/news_img/2117690191783796736/yF0xcG2t?format=jpg&name=150x150", "width": 150}], "start": 165, "status": 200, "title": "Fisher and Resende in Brazil", "unwound_url": "https://www.grumpy-economist.com/p/fisher-and-resende-in-brazil", "url": "https://t.co/x9lrkGNc2l"}]}, "id": "2117710081190203612", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 2, "impression_count": 1667, "like_count": 11, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 1, "retweet_count": 2}, "text": "Worth reading @JohnHCochrane's thoughts on what to do about Brazil's notorious combination of usuriously high real interest rates + minimal primary budget deficits\n\nhttps://t.co/x9lrkGNc2l", "url": "https://x.com/M_C_Klein/status/2117710081190203612"}, {"author_id": "497231011", "created_at": "2026-11-03T19:50:13.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2117705931521679695"], "entities": {"hashtags": [{"end": 7, "start": 1, "tag": "China"}], "urls": [{"description": "Data brokers used property listings and sham job ads to supply overseas buyers, exposing citizens to telecom and online scams", "display_url": "caixinglobal.com/2026-11-03/chi…", "end": 251, "expanded_url": "https://www.caixinglobal.com/2026-11-03/china-prosecutors-detail-data-sale-networks-linked-to-overseas-scams-102500258.html", "images": [{"height": 373, "url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/news_img/2117705974773338112/3vCmlHzE?format=jpg&name=orig", "width": 560}, {"height": 150, "url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/news_img/2117705974773338112/3vCmlHzE?format=jpg&name=150x150", "width": 150}], "start": 228, "status": 200, "title": "China Prosecutors Detail Data-Sale Networks Linked to Overseas Scams", "unwound_url": "https://www.caixinglobal.com/2026-11-03/china-prosecutors-detail-data-sale-networks-linked-to-overseas-scams-102500258.html", "url": "https://t.co/baGxrQaNoo"}]}, "id": "2117705931521679695", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 958, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "\"#China’s top prosecutorial agency said domestic criminal networks sold Chinese citizens’ personal info to overseas buyers, exposing one route by which cross-border telecom &amp; online fraudsters obtain data to target victims\"\nhttps://t.co/baGxrQaNoo", "url": "https://x.com/ChinaBeigeBook/status/2117705931521679695"}, {"author_id": "733647469305864195", "created_at": "2026-11-03T19:31:02.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2117701103072801059"], "entities": {"urls": [{"display_url": "x.com/Richard_Casey/…", "end": 268, "expanded_url": "https://twitter.com/Richard_Casey/status/2117541929961283773", "start": 245, "url": "https://t.co/mdSBaQVZRS"}]}, "id": "2117701103072801059", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 5, "impression_count": 6141, "like_count": 15, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 3, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2117541929961283773", "type": "quoted"}], "text": "China has a bit of a choice.   The RMB appreciation of the last year plus reversed the real depreciation that came from following the dollar down after liberation day, but nothing more -- it hasn't reversed the structural undervaluation ...\n\n1/ https://t.co/mdSBaQVZRS", "url": "https://x.com/Brad_Setser/status/2117701103072801059"}, {"author_id": "2961589380", "created_at": "2026-11-03T18:04:24.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2117679298534342981"], "entities": {"mentions": [{"end": 212, "id": "497266110", "start": 197, "username": "BairdStrategas"}], "urls": [{"display_url": "pic.x.com/6W8isF7TJy", "end": 236, "expanded_url": "https://x.com/LizAnnSonders/status/2117679298534342981/photo/1", "media_key": "3_2117679295636086784", "start": 213, "url": "https://t.co/6W8isF7TJy"}]}, "id": "2117679298534342981", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 52, "impression_count": 20561, "like_count": 177, "quote_count": 7, "reply_count": 44, "retweet_count": 55}, "text": "For all the forward-looking concern about fate of data centers, reality is already with us: data center project cancellations in 3Q alone were almost larger than entirety of 2025 and 2024 combined\n@BairdStrategas https://t.co/6W8isF7TJy", "url": "https://x.com/LizAnnSonders/status/2117679298534342981"}, {"author_id": "702235316812275712", "created_at": "2026-11-03T17:52:02.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2117676188357496843"], "entities": {"urls": [{"display_url": "x.com/EconBerger/sta…", "end": 279, "expanded_url": "https://twitter.com/EconBerger/status/2117634430135304251", "start": 256, "url": "https://t.co/MzqFP7fjfm"}]}, "id": "2117676188357496843", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 1331, "like_count": 1, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2117634430135304251", "type": "quoted"}], "text": "There's been genuine but minor improvement in hiring, quits and layoffs this year.\n\nBut if you got really excited about September's solid JOLTS data or July/August's more disappointing data, you're almost certainly overreacting to noise in both directions https://t.co/MzqFP7fjfm", "url": "https://x.com/EconBerger/status/2117676188357496843"}, {"author_id": "702235316812275712", "created_at": "2026-11-03T17:31:33.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2117671034644299878"], "entities": {"urls": [{"display_url": "x.com/EconBerger/sta…", "end": 303, "expanded_url": "https://twitter.com/EconBerger/status/2116151581087572150", "start": 280, "url": "https://t.co/YGS4VguOnJ"}]}, "id": "2117671034644299878", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 3, "impression_count": 1778, "like_count": 13, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 6, "retweet_count": 1}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2116151581087572150", "type": "quoted"}], "text": "Since we're probably going to see \"why is wage growth cooling?\" takes on Friday, reminder that:\n\n1/ most of the measured cooling is probably a composition effect, not \"true\" wage growth cooling\n\n2/ comp cost growth isn't cooling at all; health insurance costs are squeezing wages https://t.co/YGS4VguOnJ", "url": "https://x.com/EconBerger/status/2117671034644299878"}, {"author_id": "14096763", "created_at": "2026-11-03T17:20:18.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2117668204424130876"], "entities": {"mentions": [{"end": 60, "id": "1261335549215989760", "start": 49, "username": "Polymarket"}]}, "id": "2117668204424130876", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 23, "impression_count": 69344, "like_count": 237, "quote_count": 2, "reply_count": 30, "retweet_count": 10}, "text": "Dems drifting a ltouch lower across the board on @Polymarket. David Jolly was at 39% at this time yesterday in FL Gov. Now down to 34%. Senate Control from 79% to 75%. Nothing too major, but reversing some of the manic Dem buying that we saw the last 36-48 hours.", "url": "https://x.com/TheStalwart/status/2117668204424130876"}, {"author_id": "961132338", "created_at": "2026-11-03T17:19:53.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2117668096068727004"], "entities": {"urls": [{"display_url": "x.com/DanaGoldstein/…"